bookmark-gt
***********

bookmark-gt extends the built-in ‘bookmark.el’ and is fully compatible
with it.  When enabled, the standard bookmark keys run the corresponding
bookmark-gt commands.  Its bookmarks are ordinary ‘bookmark.el’ records,
thus a bookmark file written by bookmark-gt can still be read by the
built-in bookmark package.

   bookmark-gt is inspired by bookmark+
(https://www.emacswiki.org/emacs/BookmarkPlus).

   bookmark-gt's main features are:

   • tags, including default tags computed from the location being
     bookmarked;
   • several bookmarks with the same name, distinguished by their
     destination;
   • a bookmark list buffer for searching, filtering and updating many
     bookmarks at once;
   • bookmarks that follow their file when it is renamed inside Emacs;
   • a jump reader that works with marginalia, vertico, consult and
     orderless;
   • temporary bookmarks, which are never saved to disk;
   • auto-update bookmarks, which keep track of where you are in a long
     document;
   • bookmark types for URLs, Dired buffers, functions, keyboard macros
     and sequences of bookmarks.

   A short demo: <https://youtu.be/hitAyO8ArYM>

