1 Install
*********

With use-package and a local checkout:

     (use-package bookmark-gt
       :straight nil
       :load-path "~/.emacs.d/modules/bookmark-gt"
       :bind (("C-x r u" . bookmark-gt-create-url)  ; bookmark a URL
              ("C-x r U" . bookmark-gt-update))     ; move a bookmark to point
       :config
       (bookmark-gt-mode 1))

   bookmark-gt requires Emacs 30.1 or later.  While ‘bookmark-gt-mode’
is on, the built-in bookmark keys are remapped to run the corresponding
bookmark-gt functions:

Key         Built-in                Runs
-----------------------------------------------------------
‘C-x r m’   ‘bookmark-set’          ‘bookmark-gt-create’
‘C-x r b’   ‘bookmark-jump’         ‘bookmark-gt-jump’
‘C-x r l’   ‘bookmark-bmenu-list’   ‘bookmark-gt-list’
‘M-x’       ‘bookmark-delete’       ‘bookmark-gt-delete’
‘M-x’       ‘bookmark-rename’       ‘bookmark-gt-rename’

   Turning the mode off restores the original key bindings.

   The following packages are optional; bookmark-gt uses them when they
are installed and works without them:

   • ‘marginalia’ adds tags, type and location to each candidate in the
     jump reader;
   • ‘orderless’ enables the ‘@type’, ‘+group’ and ‘;tag’ narrowing
     particles in the jump reader;
   • ‘browser-gt’ is required only by ‘bookmark-gt-browser-tabs-mode’.

