File: bookmark-gt.info,  Node: Columns,  Next: Keys,  Up: The *Bookmarks-gt List* buffer

3.1.1 Columns
-------------

Col   Header   Meaning
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
0     ‘*’      ‘*’ if the row is marked with ‘m’, ‘D’ if it is flagged for deletion with ‘d’
1     ‘^’      ‘^’ if the bookmark has the ‘auto-update’ property
2     ‘t’      ‘t’ if the bookmark is temporary
3     Name     The name, truncated at ‘bookmark-gt-list-name-width’ (default 32)
4     Type     File, URL, EWW, Dired, Info, Org, PDF, BrowserTab, Function, Sequence, Kmacro, BkView, ...
5     Group    Web, File, Doc, Code, Media or Other
6     Tags     The tags, separated by commas, truncated at ‘bookmark-gt-list-tags-width’ (default 24)
7     Loc      The file name, or the URL for a bookmark without a file

   The name of a bookmark whose file no longer exists is shown struck
through (face ‘bookmark-gt-face-missing-file’).  Remote (Tramp) files
are not checked.


File: bookmark-gt.info,  Node: Keys,  Next: Acting on several bookmarks at once,  Prev: Columns,  Up: The *Bookmarks-gt List* buffer

3.1.2 Keys
----------

Key          Action
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
‘RET’        Jump
‘o’, ‘C-o’   Jump in another window
‘TAB’        Show the bookmark in another window, leaving point in the list
‘m’          Mark the row (with a numeric prefix, mark N rows)
‘u’          Unmark the row
‘U’          Unmark every row
‘d’          Flag the row for deletion
‘x’          Delete the flagged rows, after confirmation
‘^’          Toggle ‘auto-update’ (selection)
‘T’          Toggle temporary (selection)
‘t e’        Edit tags as a comma-separated list, adding and removing in one prompt (selection)
‘t a’        Add tags, one per prompt; empty ‘RET’ or ‘M-RET’ ends (selection)
‘t r’        Remove tags, completing over the tags present (selection)
‘r’          Rename
‘R’          Relocate: change the file name or URL
‘a’          Edit the annotation
‘i’          Show the record
‘H’          Show or hide temporary bookmarks in this buffer
‘/’          Filter by type, group, tag or name regexp, or remove the filters
‘s’          Cycle the sort column
‘V’          Reset the view: sort by name, no filters, default display of temporary bookmarks
‘g’          Refresh browser tabs and auto-update positions (if those modes are on), then redraw
‘C-x C-s’    Save the bookmark file
‘q’          Quit

   Marks belong to the bookmark, not to the line, so they are kept when
the buffer is sorted, reverted or redrawn after a change.


