‘bookmark-gt-list-selection-mark’         ‘?*’                                                                 Character shown for rows marked with ‘m’.
‘bookmark-gt-list-deletion-mark’          ‘?D’                                                                 Character shown for rows flagged with ‘d’.
‘bookmark-gt-list-default-show-temp’      ‘t’                                                                  Whether a new list buffer shows temporary bookmarks; ‘H’ changes it per buffer.
‘bookmark-gt-list-persist-state’          ‘nil’                                                                Whether the list buffer's view is saved across sessions.
‘bookmark-gt-jump-name-max-width’         ‘58’                                                                 Width at which the jump reader truncates names, so that long names leave room for the annotation.
‘bookmark-gt-jump-location-max-width’     ‘100’                                                                Limit on the width of the location in the jump annotation: columns (integer), a fraction of ‘marginalia-field-width’ (float), or no limit (nil).
‘bookmark-gt-jump-default-sort’           ‘mru’                                                                Sort order of ‘bookmark-gt-jump’ when ‘:sort-by’ is not given: ‘mru’, ‘visits’, or nil for the list's order.
‘bookmark-gt-dired-virtual-max-size’      ‘524288’                                                             Largest virtual Dired listing, in bytes, that a bookmark can store.
‘bookmark-gt-auto-update-interval’        ‘60’                                                                 Seconds of idle time between updates of auto-update bookmarks.
‘bookmark-gt-track-renames’               ‘t’                                                                  Whether renaming a file updates the bookmarks pointing at it.
‘bookmark-gt-default-tags’                ‘nil’                                                                Tags proposed by ‘bookmark-gt-default-tags-mode’: a string, a list of strings, or a function of the record.
‘bookmark-gt-prompt-for-tags-flag’        ‘t’                                                                  Whether creating a bookmark interactively prompts for tags; default tags and ‘bookmark-gt-create-tag-reader-hook’ apply either way.
‘bookmark-gt-allow-same-name-bookmarks’   ‘different-destination’                                              When a new bookmark may reuse a name: ‘never’, ‘different-destination’ or ‘always’.
‘bookmark-gt-unique-names’                ‘("\\`org-capture-last-stored\\'" "\\`org-refile-last-stored\\'")’   Regexps of names that always identify a single bookmark, whatever the previous option says.
‘bookmark-gt-unique-name-handlers’        ‘(burly-bookmark-handler)’                                           Handlers whose bookmarks are one per name: storing one replaces the existing bookmark of that name and handler.
‘bookmark-gt-auto-temp-names’             ‘("\\`org-capture-last-stored\\'" "\\`org-refile-last-stored\\'")’   Regexps of names whose bookmarks are made temporary when stored.
‘bookmark-gt-highlight-enable’            ‘t’                                                                  Whether bookmarks are highlighted in the buffers visiting their files.
‘bookmark-gt-file-type-handlers’          ‘nil’                                                                File-name regexps mapped to the functions that open matching file bookmarks.
‘bookmark-gt-browser-tabs-browsers’       ‘nil’                                                                Browser clients asked for tabs, such as ‘("chrome" "firefox")’; nil asks every connected browser.
‘bookmark-gt-browser-tabs-filter’         ‘nil’                                                                Which tabs to keep: nil for all, a regexp the URL must match, or a predicate called with the tab.


