10 Acknowledgements
*******************

bookmark-gt owes a great deal to Drew Adams
(https://www.emacswiki.org/emacs/DrewsElispLibraries) and his bookmark+
(https://www.emacswiki.org/emacs/BookmarkPlus) package, in design and in
code.  Most of its features (tags, URL, EWW, region, function, sequence
and keyboard-macro bookmarks, temporary bookmarks, visit tracking,
highlighting and filtering by tag) first appeared in bookmark+.

   The URL handler (‘bookmark-gt-handler-url-jump’) and the Dired
handler (‘bookmark-gt-handler-dired-jump’) were adapted from bookmark+'s
‘bmkp-jump-url-browse’ and ‘bmkp-jump-dired’.  The record keys ‘tags’,
‘bmkp-temp’, ‘auto-update’, ‘visits’, ‘last-visited’, ‘location’,
‘front-context-region-string’ and ‘rear-context-region-string’ are
bookmark+'s, so these fields are kept when a bookmark file is used by
both packages.  The one exception is the ‘" - no file -"’ placeholder,
which bookmark-gt reads but does not write (see *note Data compatibility
with bookmark+::); whether bookmark+ accepts a record without ‘filename’
has not been tested.

   bookmark-gt is a rewrite, not a fork: it is built on
‘tabulated-list-mode’ and on registries of handlers, groups, filters and
sort orders.  Its features, its design ideas and the handler code it
adapts come from Drew's work.


